\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Investors lament lost opportunity after unconvincing Turkish rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2023\par 17:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates lira's fresh record low and bond prices in paragraph 9)\par \par \uc2 By Libby George\par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 23 (Reuters) - Foreign investors hoping for a game-changing rate hike from Turkey's newly appointed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said Thursday's disappointing move to a key rate of just 15% could keep some money on the sidelines.\par \par \uc2 The appointment of U.S.-trained banker \uc2 Hafize Gaye Erkan\uc2  to lead the bank boosted expectations that it would rapidly raise rates to unravel years of unorthodox policies as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 But the 650 basis point hike - to 15% - was well below the median rate expectation in a Reuters poll of a rise to 21%, leaving some fretting that Erkan might have limited room to aggressively tackle inflation.\par \par \uc2 "They lost one perfect chance to demonstrate that they mean business," said Viktor Szabo, emerging markets investment director with \uc2 Abrdn\uc2 . "Whether it's because they have political constraints, or they're afraid for the banking system, it's not great. It's not a great message."\par \par \uc2 Newly re-elected President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , a self-described enemy of high interest rates, for years directed a heavily managed economic system, with a tightly controlled lira, rate cuts in the face of galloping inflation and plentiful credit for local borrowers.\par \par \uc2 Amidst tumbling reserves and fleeing investors, his choice of Erkan at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and investor darling \uc2 Mehmet Simsek\uc2  as finance minister, prompted bets for a quick turnaround to unravel some of these policies.\par \par \uc2 But analysts said that after Thursday's decision, Erkan and Simsek would need to work even harder to prove the country had indeed shifted course.\par \par \uc2 "They look less credible now," \uc2 Eric Fine\uc2 , portfolio manager of emerging market debt at VanEck, said of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding: "They need to hike rates to whatever level prevents the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  using reserves. They haven't."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lira suffered a second consecutive day of declines on Friday, hitting a fresh record low of 25.74 to the dollar before retracing, while the country's international bonds eked out small gains after tumbling on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Already in the week to June 16, foreign investor holdings of Turkish government bonds had fallen by $16.2 million.\par \par \uc2 "For now, it's not enough, probably, for long-term investors. Because of the magnitude of some of the problems in the economy," said Marek Drimal, a lead strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CAUTION AND TEMPERED DISAPPOINTMENT\par \par \uc2 Still, many, including Drimal, saw positive signs, and noted that even Simsek had repeatedly said that gradual rate moves were move likely.\par \par \uc2 Simsek also promised predictable, market-based economic policies and an inflation-targeting model would enable capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 "I think investor disappointment should be tempered," said Dan Wood, portfolio manager at William Blair, adding that the bank also signalled that it will keep hiking rates until inflation improved.\par \par \uc2 "It is clearly positive that a return to a more orthodox economic policy has been signalled."\par \par \uc2 The associate director of ratings agency Scope Ratings and a sovereign analyst at ratings agency \uc2 Fitch\uc2  also said the hike itself was positive - but the core question would be whether Erdogan allows Erkan to stay the course with continued rises.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think investors will throw in the towel just yet because I think there is still expectation there is more to come in the coming months," said Kaan Nazli, portfolio manager at \uc2 Neuberger Berman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The market is very cautious - so to regain confidence, that will take a long time. I would think that you would need to maintain tight policy for a considerable amount of time for significant, more long-term inflows to come in." (Additional reporting by Karin Strohecker and Marc Jones; Editing by Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-23T16:59:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230623ej6n02apt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
