\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish Stocks, Bonds Slide as Election Appears Headed to Runoff -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chelsey Dulaney \par \uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2023\par 11:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Turkish stocks and bond prices fell after an inconclusive presidential election result that sets the stage for a runoff ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/having-established-turkey-on-the-world-stage-erdogan-faces-risky-vote-at-home-fd0793d9?mod=hpleadpos8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/having-established-turkey-on-the-world-stage-erdogan-faces-risky-vote-at-home-fd0793d9?mod=hpleadpos8}}}\uc2 ) later this month.\par \par \uc2 With more than 91% of votes counted, incumbent President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  had won 49.49% of votes, while rival \uc2 Kemal Kilicdaroglu\uc2  claimed 44.7%, Turkey's election chief said. Neither candidate reached the 50% threshold required to avoid a runoff, which would take place on May 28.\par \par \uc2 In recent market action: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Stocks fell. The benchmark \f28 \uc2 \f2 Borsa Istanbul\f28 \uc2 \f2  100 Index was recently down \par       2.7%, after falling as much as 6.7% earlier in the session. \par  \par    -- Bond prices declined, sending yields higher. The yield on a \par       dollar-denominated government bond due 2030 rose to 9.268%, up from \par       8.059% on Friday, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tradeweb\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Yields and prices move \par       inversely. \par  \par    -- The lira weakened. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped 0.2% against the dollar. Analysts \par       said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stem \par       the lira's decline. \par  \par    -- Investors bought protection against a government default. It now costs \par       $606 a year to insure $10,000 of sovereign debt against default, as \par       measured by 5-year credit-default swaps, data from S&P Global Market \par       Intelligence showed, up from $492 on Friday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The results make it almost impossible for the opposition to overcome," said Gustavo Medeiros, head of research at emerging market-focused investment firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ashmore\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Mr. Erdogan's ruling alliance was also on track for a majority in parliament.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors have pulled money out of Turkey under the rule of Mr. Erdogan, who has pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to adopt an unorthodox policy of cutting interest rates despite soaring inflation. The lira has lost more than half its value in the past two years despite repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that have depleted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Turkey\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign reserves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors say if Mr. Erdogan is reelected, the Turkish economy could be headed for a reckoning over its imbalances, which include a wide current-account deficit and a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that is still overvalued.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Turkey has always had vulnerabilities but for the past three years the country has increasingly been on borrowed time," said Richard Briggs, a senior fund manager at Candriam, in emailed comments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If Turkey continues to run large current-account deficits...pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the economy could be severe without a credible policy framework which is less likely under the existing administration," Mr. Briggs said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTE: In-line links reference additional content of interest chosen by the WSJ news team.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This item is part of a Wall Street Journal live coverage event. The full stream can be found by searching P/WSJL (WSJ Live Coverage).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 15, 2023 05:24 ET (09:24 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230515ej5f001f6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
