\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rallies after Fed signals pause\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2023\par 11:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China's skidding factory sector taps brakes on economic recovery\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds interest rates\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 GS cautious on Turkish bank stocks ahead of election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fall in inflation slower than expected - \uc2 Turkish c.bank\uc2  governor\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  up 0.2%, stocks add 0.7%\par \par \uc2 By Bansari Mayur Kamdar\par \par \uc2 May 4 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Thursday, supported by a weaker dollar after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  opened its doors to a pause in rate hikes, while the Turkish lira was subdued after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stuck to its 2023 inflation forecast.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI's index for emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 0.2% by 0825 GMT, after the Fed raised rates by a quarter of a percentage point on Wednesday in what may be its last in a historic series of hikes in the world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Regional stocks added 0.7%.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index gained 1.3%, helped by a 4.8% rally in banking stocks.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its main policy rate, even as weakness in its pegged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forced the city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to deplete banking system cash to 15-year lows.\par \par \uc2 China's blue-chip CSI300 Index closed flat and the Shanghai Composite Index added 0.8% as trading resumed after the May Day holiday break.\par \par \uc2 China's factory activity unexpectedly dipped in April, a private sector survey showed, due to softer domestic demand and suggesting the manufacturing sector is losing momentum amid a bumpy post-COVID recovery.\par \par \uc2 Among emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the South African rand inched up 0.1% against the greenback, while Turkey's lira was flat.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's inflation is falling at a slower rate than expected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Governor \uc2 Sahap Kavcioglu\uc2 , adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains Turkey's inflation forecast of 22.3% for 2023.\par \par \uc2 "The lira is not trading at all on market dynamics and macroeconomics fundamentals," said Ipek Ozkardeskaya, a senior analyst at \uc2 Swissquote Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Right now, it is really driven by very heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even more so these days in order to manage a potentially higher selling pressure on the lira before the May 14 Presidential elections."\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said it was cautious on Turkish banks heading into the elections, with lenders more vulnerable than the country's other stocks to a potential post-vote rate hike following years of unorthodox monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Russia's rouble rose to a near one-month high at 79.03 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Hungarian forint rose 0.5% against the euro, leading gains in central and eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Czech crown added 0.1% a day after the \uc2 Czech National Bank\uc2  voted 4-3 to keep the key policy rate at 7.00%.\par \par \uc2 High borrowing costs threaten the Hungarian economy and risk a credit crunch, the economic development minister said, adding that inflation needed to fall so that interest rates can come down.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday held interest rates steady for a sixth consecutive policy meeting and said it was "less likely" to resume hikes.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  is preparing to discuss Pakistan's budget plans for the coming financial year, as part of a long-awaited bailout tranche from the lender for the cash-strapped country. (Reporting by Bansari Mayur Kamdar in Bengaluru; Editing by Subhranshu Sahu) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-4T10:04:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230504ej5401lpz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
