\par\par \b \uc2 METAIR INVESTMENTS LIMITED\uc2  - Voluntary  \highlight22\uc2 operational \highlight\uc2  update\b0\par\par\uc2 1,327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2022\par 09:00\par \uc2 Johannesburg Stock Exchange\par \uc2 JSEXCH\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2022 Johannesburg Stock Exchange. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Voluntary \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  update\par \par \uc2 METAIR INVESTMENTS LIMITED\par \par \uc2 (Incorporated in the Republic of South Africa)\par \par \uc2 Registration number: 1948/031013/06\par \par \uc2 JSE\uc2  share code: \uc2 MTA\par \par \uc2 (\u8220\'20\'1CMetair\u8221\'20\'1D or the \u8220\'20\'1CGroup\u8221\'20\'1D)\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTARY \b \highlight22\uc2 OPERATIONAL\b0 \highlight\uc2  UPDATE\par \par \uc2 The Automotive Components Vertical and Energy Storage Vertical are performing well relative to their\par \par \uc2 challenging operating environments. Key projects remain on track in the Automotive Components\par \par \uc2 Vertical despite the impact of global supply chain disruptions, semi-conductor shortages and shipping\par \par \uc2 constraints, including \uc2 Transnet\uc2  port disruptions. The Energy Storage Vertical continues to deliver strong\par \par \uc2 automotive battery volumes and revenues despite the Turkish and Romanian \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  navigating\par \par \uc2 through short term inflationary cost pressures and the ongoing war in Ukraine. Inflation in Turkey rose\par \par \uc2 dramatically during the first half of the year, as indicated during the interim reporting period, with the\par \par \uc2 annual inflation rate reaching 85.5% in October 2022. Despite the ongoing economic challenges in\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC remains resilient with management \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  yielding positive results.\par \par \uc2 Automotive Components Vertical\par \par \uc2 The temporary suspension of production at Toyota South Africa Manufacturing (\u8220\'20\'1CToyota SA\u8221\'20\'1D), following\par \par \uc2 the severe flooding in KwaZulu-Natal (\u8220\'20\'1CKZN\u8221\'20\'1D) in April 2022, impacted the South African \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 significantly, however production levels resumed during September 2022 and have stabilised at pre-\par \par \uc2 flood levels. The recovery of the Toyota SA Prospecton plant, which was severely damaged by floods,\par \par \uc2 is a huge accomplishment by Toyota SA and was critical to the wider industry, specifically suppliers\par \par \uc2 from the automotive component manufacturing sector. The Group business interruption insurance claim\par \par \uc2 progressed well with R400 million in cash received to date. The total claim is capped at R500 million\par \par \uc2 and is expected to be finalised in January 2023, with the final claim currently under review by the\par \par \uc2 insurers.\par \par \uc2 Production of the Group\u8217\'20\'19s major new model investment, the next-generation Ford Ranger, commenced\par \par \uc2 on Wednesday, 16 November 2022 at \uc2 Ford\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Silverton assembly plant. \uc2 Metair\uc2  subsidiaries have entered\par \par \uc2 production and ramp-up phases with peak production levels planned from January 2023. The vertical\par \par \uc2 expects to incur pre-production and engineering (project) cash costs of up to R475 million related to the\par \par \uc2 new model in FY2022, of which we expect at least 35% will be capitalised.\par \par \uc2 Raw material shortages (including semi-conductor chips), supply chain delays and the loss of \uc2 Toyota\par \par \uc2 SA production time due to the KZN flooding have impacted Original Equipment Manufacturer (\u8220\'20\'1COEM\u8221\'20\'1D)\par \par \uc2 volumes. While there is a degree of uncertainty around the short-term volume fluctuation for the\par \par \uc2 remainder of the year, volume expectations over the model lives remain unchanged. \uc2 Metair\uc2  expects\par \par \uc2 2022 industry OEM production volumes to be ahead of 2021 volumes, at c.550 000 cars, which\par \par \uc2 represents c. 90% of 2019 (pre-Covid) volumes. \uc2 Metair\uc2  expects OEM production volumes to be\par \par \uc2 progressively increasing in excess of c. 700,000 from 2023, subject to supply chain stability.\par \par \uc2 Management \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the impact of short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressures are in place and\par \par \uc2 ongoing investments are expected to deliver returns in line with \uc2 Metair\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s targets over the life of the\par \par \uc2 contracts. New model and facelift launches are expected to drive meaningful growth over the medium\par \par \uc2 to long term, most notably the ongoing contract into \uc2 Ford\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investment into the South African automotive\par \par \uc2 industry, supporting incremental revenue for the Metair Group of an estimated R46bn over model life.\par \par \uc2 Energy Storage Vertical\par \par \uc2 The Energy Storage Vertical continues to perform resiliently under tough operating conditions, including\par \par \uc2 high inflation fuelled by unprecedented energy and labour cost increases across both Turkey and\par \par \uc2 Romania. Although these costs have generally been recovered from customers following a slight time\par \par \uc2 lag, margins have been negatively impacted in the short term. Market demand has remained strong\par \par \uc2 and international demand for lead acid batteries across all sales channels, but especially Turkey,\par \par \uc2 remains resilient. Hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  export sales provide a natural hedge to limit the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 The last quarter of the calendar year is the most volume sensitive time for the business and final annual\par \par \uc2 volumes will depend on the final sales volumes achieved in this last quarter. Currently, total automotive\par \par \uc2 battery volumes sold are expected to reach between 8.5 million and 9.0 million units for the full year, as\par \par \uc2 we anticipate Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC export volumes increasing by at least 17% from FY2021. Volumes from Rombat\par \par \uc2 are expected to be c. 15% lower mainly due to dampened consumer confidence from the ongoing\par \par \uc2 conflict in Ukraine. With efforts to improve competitiveness and market share progressing, sales\par \par \uc2 volumes for First National Battery in South Africa are expected to be on par with FY2021.\par \par \uc2 Hyperinflation in Turkey\par \par \uc2 As previously reported, the Group applies hyperinflationary accounting (IAS 29) for amounts reported\par \par \uc2 by Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC in Turkey. Under IAS 29, Turkish Lira results and non-monetary asset and liability\par \par \uc2 balances (including undistributed profits) are restated to present value equivalent local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 amounts (adjusted based on CPI) before translation to ZAR at reporting-date exchange rate. Although\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain unchanged, with a substantial portion of commodity input costs and sales being hard\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated and not directly subject to Turkish inflation, as well as Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC\u8217\'20\'19s strong non-\par \par \uc2 monetary asset base, the accounting impact on profit and loss is negative as IAS 29 requires the\par \par \uc2 restatement of Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC\u8217\'20\'19s retained income within current year earnings. Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC continues to grow\par \par \uc2 both volumes and prices in FY2022, and strategies are in place to manage hyperinflation \b \highlight22\uc2 operationally\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Turkey\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its benchmark interest rate by 1.5 percentage points to 9% despite\par \par \uc2 the country\u8217\'20\'19s high inflation rate, the Turkish banking system has not passed on the lower interest rates\par \par \uc2 to customers due to the high inflation. Although there are currently no restrictions on remittances of\par \par \uc2 dividends from Turkey and access to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains unrestricted, the Turkish government\par \par \uc2 has issued new banking regulations which include a rule that forces exporters to sell 40% of their\par \par \uc2 foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenue to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Mutlu Ak\u252\'00\'FC has assessed the impact of the financial\par \par \uc2 regulations and is developing measures to minimise interest rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatilities.\par \par \uc2 Financial position\par \par \uc2 The Group is in a satisfactory financial position to support current expansion projects, and has the\par \par \uc2 required lending facilities in place to support \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as the expansion programmes. The\par \par \uc2 consequences of supply chain disruptions and availability of raw materials have necessitated a greater\par \par \uc2 inventory holding strategy to mitigate shipping delays and airfreight costs. The Group formally received\par \par \uc2 the covenant waiver from lenders and adjustments to the covenant calculations, mainly for\par \par \uc2 hyperinflation (IAS 29) impacts are under consideration.\par \par \uc2 Value unlock opportunities\par \par \uc2 Metair\uc2  continues to actively work towards value unlock opportunities in the short and long term within\par \par \uc2 both business Verticals. The consideration of a value unlock process within Energy Storage for\par \par \uc2 stakeholders has not translated into an executable transaction, largely due to the geopolitical climate\par \par \uc2 within Eastern Europe. The Board will revisit its strategic options as and when the operating climate\par \par \uc2 improves.\par \par \uc2 In the interim, \uc2 Metair\uc2  remains focused on maximising the value potential of the Energy Storage vertical\par \par \uc2 and on executing on the growth and expansion opportunities available for the Automotive Components\par \par \uc2 vertical.\par \par \uc2 The information contained in this announcement is the responsibility of the directors of \uc2 Metair\uc2  and does\par \par \uc2 not constitute an earnings forecast. Such information has not been audited, reviewed, or reported on\par \par \uc2 by the Group\u8217\'20\'19s external auditors.\par \par \uc2 5 December 2022\par \par \uc2 Johannesburg\par \par \uc2 Sponsor\par \par \uc2 One Capital\par \par \uc2 Date: 05-12-2022 08:00:00\par \par \uc2 Produced by the JSE SENS Department. The SENS service is an information dissemination service administered by the \uc2 JSE Limited\uc2  ('\uc2 JSE\uc2 ').\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 JSE\uc2  does not, whether expressly, tacitly or implicitly, represent, warrant or in any way guarantee the truth, accuracy or completeness of\par \par \uc2 the information published on SENS. The \uc2 JSE\uc2 , their officers, employees and agents accept no liability for (or in respect of) any direct,\par \par \uc2 indirect, incidental or consequential loss or damage of any kind or nature, howsoever arising, from the use of SENS or the use of, or reliance on,\par \par \uc2 information disseminated through SENS.\par \par \uc2 Dokument JSEXCH0020221205eic500008\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
