\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Fitch\uc2  cuts Turkey's debt ratings to 'B' from 'B+'\b0\par\par\uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2022\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details from statement)\par \par \uc2 July 8 (Reuters) - Ratings agency \uc2 Fitch\uc2  downgraded Turkey's debt rating to "B" from "B+" on Friday, citing increasing inflation and broad concerns about the economy, from a widening current account deficit to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  shot to a 24-year high 78.62% in June, mainly due to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis at the end of last year and the lira's continued decline.\par \par \uc2 The economic fallout from Russia's invasion of Ukraine has also stoked prices in import-dependent Turkey, especially due to rising energy and commodity costs.\par \par \uc2 In a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/research/sovereigns/fitch-downgrades-turkiye-to-b-outlook-negative-08-07-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , the agency affirmed its ratings outlook at "negative", adding that it expects Turkey's consumption to slow given rising inflation, a weaker exchange rate and diminishing domestic confidence.\par \par \uc2 Fitch\uc2  forecast annual inflation to average 71.4% this year, the highest among sovereigns rated by the agency, adding that its trajectory remains highly uncertain. Average inflation is set to slow to 57% in 2023, \uc2 Fitch\uc2  said, due to overly accommodative policies until parliamentary and presidential elections scheduled for no later than June 2023.\par \par \uc2 The lira lost 44% of its value against the dollar last year, mainly due to a series of rate cuts from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sought by President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is down a further 23% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The government has taken steps to stem the lira's decline. A recent move by the BDDK banking watchdog to restrict lira lending to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rich companies helped it rally briefly last week as corporates sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Referring to the move, \uc2 Fitch\uc2  said "policies are becoming increasingly \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as unpredictable."\par \par \uc2 Last year's rate cuts were part of Erdogan's new economic programme, which prioritises exports, production and investments, while keeping lending costs low.\par \par \uc2 The policy rate has stood at 14% since December, leaving real yields in deeply negative territory.\par \par \uc2 One of the goals was to turn Turkey's chronic current account deficits to a surplus, but those plans were derailed as energy and commodity prices soared due to the Ukraine conflict, sharply widening Turkey's trade deficit.\par \par \uc2 "The government's focus on maintaining high growth feeds \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand, depreciation pressures on the lira, decline in international reserves and spiralling inflation, and discourages capital inflows to fund the higher current account deficit," \uc2 Fitch\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It forecast the current account deficit at 5.1% of gross domestic product this year, due to the higher energy prices and weakened external demand, despite a recovery in tourism.\par \par \uc2 The agency also cited the continued pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves despite measures introduced to replenish them. As of July 1, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves remained near a 20-year low at $7.51 billion. (Reporting by Vansh Agarwal in Bengaluru and Ali Kucukgocmen in Istanbul; Editing by Shailesh Kuber and william Mallard) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-9T06:15:49.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220708ei7803q11\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
