\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 Fitch\uc2  Affirms Garanti BBVA at 'B'; Outlook Negative\b0\par\par\uc2 3,677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 18:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  : \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  -London-31 March 2022: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  has affirmed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkiye Garanti Bankasi A.S \f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s (Garanti \f28 \uc2 \f2 BBVA\f28 \uc2 \f2  ) Long-Term Foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (LTFC) Issuer Default Rating (IDR) at 'B', and Long-Term Local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (LTLC) IDR at 'B+'. The Outlooks are Negative, mirroring that on the sovereign. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch\f28 \uc2 \f2  has also affirmed the bank's Viability Rating (VR) at 'b+' and removed it from Rating Watch Negative (RWN).\f28 \par \par \uc2 The affirmation of the VR, one notch above Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's LTFC IDR, and the removal from RWN reflect the bank's solid FC liquidity buffer and the fact that transfer, convertibility and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks are captured in its LTFC IDR but not in its VR. \uc2 Fitch\uc2  placed Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's VR on RWN in February 2022 following the Turkish sovereign downgrade (see "\uc2 Fitch\uc2  Downgrades 22 Turkish Banks' Ratings; Outlooks Negative" on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2 ), reflecting heightened risks to its standalone credit profile amid market volatility.\par \par \uc2 Key Rating Drivers\par \par \uc2 LT IDRS, SHAREHOLDER SUPPORT RATING (SSR) AND SENIOR DEBT RATINGS\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's LTFC IDR and senior debt rating are capped at 'B', one notch below \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's LTFC IDR. This reflects our view of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk and our assessment that weaknesses in \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external finances, amid high sector deposit dollarisation and high short-term maturing FC debt in volatile market conditions, make some form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that would impede the bank's ability to service its FC obligations more likely than a sovereign default. The Negative Outlook on the LTFC IDR mirrors that on the sovereign.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, Garanti BBVA 's SSR is capped at 'b', reflecting government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, despite the bank's strategic importance to, and integration with its controlling and 49.9% shareholder, \uc2 Banco Bilbao Vizcaya Argentaria S.A\uc2  . (\uc2 BBVA\uc2  ; BBB+/Stable).\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's LTLC IDR of is one notch above its LTFC IDR, reflecting our view of a lower likelihood of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in LC. At 'B+', this rating is driven by shareholder support but underpinned by the bank's VR.\par \par \uc2 The Negative Outlooks on the bank's LTLC IDR mirrors that on the sovereign.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's senior debt ratings are aligned with its respective IDRs and reflect average recovery prospects in case of default.\par \par \uc2 VR\par \par \uc2 The affirmation of Garanti BBVA 's 'b+' VR, one notch above its LTFC IDR and the operating environment score, reflects the bank's record of resilient financial metrics underpinned by its solid domestic franchise (end-2021: 9-10% of sector assets and deposits) and significant FC liquidity and reasonable capital buffers.\par \par \uc2 Risks to the bank's credit profile remain significant, given its concentration in the volatile and challenging Turkish market. \uc2 Fitch\uc2  has downgraded the operating environment score for Turkish banks to 'b'/negative' signaling increased risks to macroeconomic and financial stability at the lower sovereign rating level. Turkish banks are vulnerable to exchange-rate volatility due to refinancing risks, given high exposure to external FC wholesale funding in a market highly sensitive to investor sentiment, high sector FC lending, given the impact on asset quality, and deposit dollarisation, due to risks to FC liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA is exposed to refinancing risks given its high, albeit declining, FC wholesale funding (end-2021: 15% of total funding). Significant deposit dollarisation also creates risks to FC liquidity in case of outflows. Nevertheless, the bank has a record of external market access, despite challenging market conditions. Furthermore, available FC liquidity (USD13.1 billion) covered the bank's maturing FC debt over 12 months (USD2.9 billion) plus over a third of FC deposits at end-2021. Nevertheless, FC liquidity could come under pressure from a prolonged loss of market access or FC deposit instability. In addition, FC liquidity largely comprises of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of Turkey\uc2  , access to which could become uncertain at times of systemic stress or material FC deposit outflows.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's reported common equity Tier 1 (CET1) ratio (13.6% at end-2021) remains at the higher end of the peer group and represents an adequate buffer over its regulatory minimum - including net of regulatory forbearance (11.3%), although its equity/assets ratio has weakened (end-2021: 9.3%) and risks to capitalisation remain from lira depreciation (given the inflation of RWAs due to high FC loans) and asset-quality pressures (given credit concentrations, among others). Nevertheless, the bank generates solid pre-impairment operating profitability (2021: about 7% of average gross loans, adjusted for hedging gains), which provides a strong buffer to absorb losses through the income statement, high impaired loans (NPL) reserves coverage and 'free provisions' against possible losses (end-2021: 1.3% of reported risk-weighted assets; RWA), underpinning the strength of its capital position.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's NPL ratio fell to 3.6% at end-2021 (end-2020: 4.4%) - a level below private bank peers' but above the sector average - despite operating environment pressures, primarily reflecting nominal loan growth, strong collections and write-offs. We expect this ratio to rise moderately in 2022, given risks to macroeconomic and financial stability and high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Stage 2 loans (17%) are the highest among large bank peers and above the sector average, although this partly reflects its conservative loan classification approach and the impact of lira depreciation (given a high share is in FC). Restructured loans (about half of Stage 2) could rise further, given macro risks. Garanti BBVA 's total reserve coverage of NPLs is the highest among peers and increased to 161% at end-2021 (end-2020: 130%) reflecting also higher coverage of Stage 3 (66%) and Stage 2 (17%) loans.\par \par \uc2 The bank's share of FC lending was a high 45% at end-2021 (sector: 42%) heightening risks, given that not all borrowers will be fully hedged against lira depreciation. These risks are somewhat mitigated since the exposures are generally to large, diversified corporates and exporters with \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues, or project finance loans carrying a government feed-in tariff (energy loans) or revenue or debt assumption guarantee.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's operating profit/ RWAs ratio (3.1% in 2021; 2.1% in 2020) is consistently among the strongest in the peer group, reflecting good margins underpinned by good funding cost optimisation and cost efficiency. \uc2 Fitch\uc2  expects Garanti BBVA to report solid profitability metrics in 2022, given its short-term negative repricing gap and the lira interest rate cuts (4Q21), while the inflationary environment should support loan volumes and CPI-linked securities income, although costs will also rise. The bank is budgeting for a moderate loan impairment charges/gross loans ratio of below 150bp in 2022 (excluding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impacts), but the uncertain macroeconomic outlook creates downside risks.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA is primarily funded by granular, retail deposits and has a higher share of demand deposits than peers. Its gross loans/deposits ratio has fallen, partly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation inflating reported FC deposits, and was a reasonable 89% at end-2021, below peers. However, FC deposits are significant (69% of total deposits, consolidated basis), and above the sector average, increasing FC liquidity risks in case of deposit instability. We expect dollarisation to remain high, notwithstanding the recently introduced \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -protected deposit scheme.\par \par \uc2 NATIONAL RATING\par \par \uc2 The affirmation of Garanti BBVA 's National Rating with a Stable Outlook reflects our view that the bank's creditworthiness in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relative to other Turkish issuers is unchanged.\par \par \uc2 SUBORDINATED DEBT RATING\par \par \uc2 The bank's subordinated debt rating of 'B-' has been affirmed. The notching for the subordinated notes includes one notch for loss severity and zero notches for non-performance risk relative to the 'B' LTFC IDR anchor rating. The one notch, rather than default two notches, for loss severity reflects our view that institutional support (as reflected in the bank's LTFC IDR) helps mitigate losses and incorporates the fact that the bank's LTFC IDR is already capped at 'B'.\par \par \uc2 Rating Sensitivities Factors that could, individually or collectively, lead to negative rating action/downgrade:\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's LTIDRs, SSR and senior debt rating are primarily sensitive to a sovereign downgrade and also to any increase in \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's view of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's SSR could be also downgraded if \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's ability and propensity to provide support reduced materially, although this is not \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's base case.\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's VR is primarily sensitive to a sovereign downgrade. \uc2 Fitch\uc2  would downgrade the VR to the level of the LTFC IDR if there was material erosion in the bank's capital and FC liquidity buffers. The VR could also be downgraded due to further marked deterioration in the operating environment, including a prolonged funding market closure or deposit instability that severely eroded the bank's FC liquidity buffer, particularly if not offset by shareholder support.\par \par \uc2 NATIONAL RATING\par \par \uc2 The National Rating is sensitive to changes in Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's LTLC IDR and its creditworthiness relative to other Turkish issuers.\par \par \uc2 SUBORDINATED DEBT\par \par \uc2 The subordinated debt rating is sensitive to a change in Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's LTFC IDR.\par \par \uc2 Factors that could, individually or collectively, lead to positive rating action/upgrade:\par \par \uc2 Upgrades of the bank's LT IDRs, SSR and senior debt rating are unlikely in the near term given the Negative Outlooks, the Negative Outlook on \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rating and \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's view of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk in the banking sector. Revision of the sovereign Outlook to Stable would reduce downward pressure on the bank's ratings, particularly if accompanied by a reduction in our view of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, and could lead to similar actions on the bank's ratings.\par \par \uc2 31 Mar 2022 12:03 ET  Press Release: \uc2 Fitch\uc2   Affirms Garanti BBVA  at 'B'; -2-\par \par \uc2 Downside pressure on the bank's VR could ease in case of marked improvement in the operating environment, likely characterised by a reduction in macroeconomic and financial volatility, and potentially also a revision of the sovereign Outlook to Stable, particularly if this reduces risks to the bank's capital and FC liquidity.\par \par \uc2 NATIONAL RATING\par \par \uc2 The National Rating is sensitive to changes in Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's LTLC IDR and its creditworthiness relative to other Turkish issuers.\par \par \uc2 SUBORDINATED DEBT\par \par \uc2 The subordinated debt rating is sensitive to a change in Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's LTFC IDR.\par \par \uc2 VR ADJUSTMENTS\par \par \uc2 The operating environment score of 'b' for Turkish banks is lower than the category implied score of 'bb', due to the following adjustment reasons: Sovereign rating (negative) and macroeconomic stability (negative). The latter adjustment reflects heightened market volatility, high dollarisation and high risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 The business profile score of 'b+' has been assigned below the implied 'bb' category implied score, due to the following adjustment reason: business model (negative). This reflects Garanti \uc2 BBVA\uc2  's business model concentration on the high-risk Turkish market.\par \par \uc2 Best/Worst Case Rating Scenario\par \par \uc2 International scale credit ratings of Financial Institutions and Covered Bond issuers have a best-case rating upgrade scenario (defined as the 99th percentile of rating transitions, measured in a positive direction) of three notches over a three-year rating horizon; and a worst-case rating downgrade scenario (defined as the 99th percentile of rating transitions, measured in a negative direction) of four notches over three years. The complete span of best- and worst-case scenario credit ratings for all rating categories ranges from 'AAA' to 'D'. Best- and worst-case scenario credit ratings are based on historical performance. For more information about the methodology used to determine sector-specific best- and worst-case scenario credit ratings, visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10111579"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10111579 }}}\par \par \uc2 Criteria Variation\par \par \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's view of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk means we view default risk of the bank as higher than that of the Turkey sovereign. As a result, we have capped the LTFC IDR at 'B', one notch below Turkey's sovereign rating. As such, \uc2 Fitch\uc2  has varied its criteria to permit a VR one notch above the bank's LTFC IDR as this is not directly capped by Turkey's Country Ceiling of 'B+', but rather our broader view of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk.\par \par \uc2 Summary of Financial Adjustments\par \par \uc2 An adjustment has been made in \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's financial spreadsheets for Garanti BBVA that has affected \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's core and complimentary metrics. \uc2 Fitch\uc2  has taken a loan classified as a financial asset measured at fair value through profit and loss in the bank's financial statements and reclassified it under gross loans as we believe this is the most appropriate line in \uc2 Fitch\uc2  spreadsheets to reflect this exposure.\par \par \uc2 REFERENCES FOR SUBSTANTIALLY MATERIAL SOURCE CITED AS KEY DRIVER OF RATING The principal sources of information used in the analysis are described in the Applicable Criteria. Public Ratings with Credit Linkage to other ratings\par \par \uc2 Garanti BBVA 's ratings are linked to the Turkish sovereign ratings and to those of the parent bank, \uc2 BBVA\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 ESG Considerations\par \par \uc2 Unless otherwise disclosed in this section, the highest level of ESG credit relevance is a score of '3'. This means ESG issues are credit-neutral or have only a minimal credit impact on the entity, either due to their nature or the way in which they are being managed by the entity. For more information on \uc2 Fitch\uc2  's ESG Relevance Scores, visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com/esg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com/esg}}}\par \par \uc2 Turkiye Garanti Bankasi A.S \uc2 .; Long Term Issuer Default Rating; Affirmed; B; Rating Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 ; Short Term Issuer Default Rating; Affirmed; B\par \par \uc2 ; Local \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Long Term Issuer Default Rating; Affirmed; B+; Rating Outlook Negative\par \par \uc2 ; Local \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Short Term Issuer Default Rating; Affirmed; B\par \par \uc2 ; National Long Term Rating; Affirmed; AA(tur); Rating Outlook Stable\par \par \uc2 ; Viability Rating; Affirmed; b+; Rating Watch Off\par \par \uc2 ; Shareholder Support Ratings; Affirmed; b\par \par \uc2 ----senior unsecured; Long Term Rating; Affirmed; B\par \par \uc2 ----subordinated; Long Term Rating; Affirmed; B-\par \par \uc2 ----senior unsecured; Long Term Rating; Affirmed; B\par \par \uc2 ----subordinated; Long Term Rating; Affirmed; B-\par \par \uc2 ----senior unsecured; Short Term Rating; Affirmed; B\par \par \uc2 Contacts:\par \par \uc2 Primary Rating Analyst\par \par \uc2 Huseyin Sevinc,\par \par \uc2 Director\par \par \uc2 +44 20 3530 1027\par \par \uc2 huseyin.sevinc@fitchratings.com\par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings Ltd\par \par \uc2 30 North Colonnade, Canary Wharf\par \par \uc2 London E14 5GN\par \par \uc2 Secondary Rating Analyst\par \par \uc2 Ahmet Kilinc,\par \par \uc2 Director\par \par \uc2 +44 20 3530 1272\par \par \uc2 ahmet.kilinc@fitchratings.com\par \par \uc2 Committee Chairperson\par \par \uc2 Redmond Ramsdale,\par \par \uc2 Senior Director\par \par \uc2 +44 20 3530 1836\