\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Erdogan  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes Turkey \highlight\uc2 's statistics agency after failing to contain inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Inflation in Turkey reached its highest level in 19 years, reaching 36.1% annually by December 2021. The result is exclusively due to the irresponsible monetary policy of President \uc2 Recep Erdogan\uc2 , who is using the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay for his political and military spending.\par \par \uc2 Actual inflation in Turkey easily exceeded the claims of the Government, which had hoped to achieve a figure close to 30% by 2021, but missed it by almost 10 points, and with inflation accelerating month by month.\par \par \uc2 In December last year alone, prices soared by 13.58% with respect to the previous month, accumulating almost a third of the annual inflation in that month, a direct path to hyperinflation.\par \par \uc2 This price increase was even higher than the monthly inflation recorded in Venezuela in the same month, and evidences the profound failure of the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 With no intention of changing course, instead of firing the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Erdogan decided to remove the president of Turkey's prestigious National Statistics Agency, Sait Erdal Dincer, from his post, just after the disastrous results of the heterodox monetary policy became known.\par \par \uc2 In his place will be Erhan Cetinkaya, who had already held several positions as banking regulator, and will fulfill Erdogan's wishes to "plug" the bad inflation numbers. Justice Minister \uc2 Abdulhamit Gul\uc2  was also dismissed for trying to oppose the president's decision.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish president did not give any kind of official and concrete explanation for his decision, and many international analysts recall the situation experienced in Argentina in October 2006 under the administration of N\u233\'00\'E9stor Kirchner, when the Argentine president \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the INDEC, dismissed Lelio M\u225\'00\'E1rmora and Graciela Bevacqua and appointed militants of his own party to falsify official statistics and artificially favor the image of his government.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish monetary policy adopted, for almost religious reasons, an absolute opposition to the adjustment of monetary policy interest rates on primary and secondary markets. This refusal prevented the relevant monetary correction after large expansion packages in 2020 as a consequence of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The government tried to compensate for its dogmatism with interest rates by including, in return, an insurance against real losses for fixed term deposits, being permanently exposed to inflation.\par \par \uc2 However, despite the initial success on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the measures were insufficient and failed to recreate confidence in the Turkish lira. Today, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on its way to a total depreciation, and many compare Turkey's inflationary spiral to that of Venezuela towards the end of \uc2 Hugo Chavez\uc2 's government.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220201ei2100az3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
