\par\par \b \uc2 Lira extends week's rally bolstered by Turkish state banks\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Dezember 2021\par 18:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL (Reuters) - Turkey's lira rallied further on Thursday and was on track for its best week in two decades, boosted by a government plan to protect some deposits and the added support of state banks aggressively selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 The lira rallied as much as 10% to 10.25 versus the dollar, its strongest level in a month, before paring most of those gains to trade at 11.395 at 1444 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has whipsawed back from a historic low of 18.4 on Monday when it was down some 60% on the year, capping a week of record volatility and intraday swings.\par \par \uc2 Despite the rebound, risk measures are near all-time highs as questions remain over the state's anti-dollarisation plan, which could further stoke inflation, add to public debt and eat into foreign reserves if the lira begins sliding again.\par \par \uc2 In an echo of past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , four sources told Reuters that \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's state banks heavily sold dollars this week after President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  announced the government would guarantee some deposits against depreciation losses.\par \par \uc2 One source said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday totalled $3 billion. The selling coincided with a drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves, which a second source said amounted to $6 billion on those two days alone.\par \par \uc2 The three big state banks - \uc2 Ziraat Bank\uc2 , Vakif Bank and Halk Bank - did not immediately comment on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not immediately available to comment.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's balance sheet suggests that $5.5 billion of the fall in net reserves on Monday and Tuesday is due to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, said Haluk Burumcekci, head of Istanbul-based Burumcekci Consulting.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting market jitters, the cost of insuring against a sovereign default using CDS broke above 600 basis points earlier this week, before dipping back to 593, still near all-time highs, according to \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 THIN RESERVES BUFFER\par \par \uc2 In 2019-2020 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  backed, via swaps, the sale of some $128 billion via state banks to stabilize the lira, depleting Turkey's foreign reserves. Earlier this year, the sales emerged as a focus of what the political opposition calls government mismanagement.\par \par \uc2 To address the latest turmoil, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has announced five direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month that bankers say totaled between $6-$10 billion. It has made no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  notices this week.\par \par \uc2 Official data shows the bank's net foreign reserves dropped to $12 billion last week, from $21 billion a week earlier, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed.\par \par \uc2 Seeking to bolster its buffer, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wrapping up talks with counterparts in Azerbaijan and the UAE on a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap line and one deal is likely before year-end, separate sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  announced the series of steps that would shift the burden of a weakened \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the Treasury and encourage Turks to hold lira rather than dollars. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will backstop lira converted from hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More than half of locals' savings is in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold, official data shows, due to a loss of confidence in the lira after years of depreciation and eroded \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility.\par \par \uc2 Under pressure from Erdogan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut rates by 500 basis points to 14% since September.\par \par \uc2 The president has pledged to continue with his low-rates policy despite widespread criticism, while opposition parties have called for immediate elections over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  meltdown.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street bank \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  said markets expect a big reversal in monetary policy and are pricing in a 16 percentage point rise in Turkey's key interest rate over the next year.\par \par \uc2 Graphic: Markets pricing in run of Turkish rate hikes next year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/gdvzymxxlpw/Pasted%20image%201640255443242.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/gdvzymxxlpw/Pasted%20image%201640255443242.png}}}\par \par \uc2 Graphic: The Erdonomics effect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/dwvkrzxozpm/Pasted%20image%201640257543003.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/dwvkrzxozpm/Pasted%20image%201640257543003.png}}}\par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Marc Jones; Editing by Jonathan Spicer and Toby Chopra) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-12-23T17:24:30.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211223ehcn0296a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\p