\par\par \b \uc2 Market Talk Roundup: Turkish Lira Rebounds After Measures Aimed at Reversing its Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 1,108 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2021\par 13:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira stages a substantial rebound on Tuesday following its recent slide to record lows, after Turkish President Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  announced measures to encourage people to hold savings in lira rather than foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts are skeptical the measures will change the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fortunes, however, unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverses course and starts raising interest rates. The following is a selection of analysts' comments.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's Plan to Encourage Lira Savings Is Likely to Prove Unsustainable\par \par \uc2 1145 GMT - Turkey's government may struggle to deliver on its plan to compensate lira deposit holders for losses resulting from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations, \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  says. "The bill for the government can easily turn out gigantic and, therefore, unsustainable," \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  strategist \uc2 Cristian Maggio\uc2  says. The government will need to ensure a "very high level" of compensation for any losses incurred by holding lira savings instead of, say, dollars, but it cannot commit to the substantial costs involved as it would risk bankrupting Turkey in a short time, he says. The lira may find some reprieve, but only temporarily, given Turkey's long-term economic weaknesses and negative inflation-adjusted real rates that could fall further as inflation accelerates and interest rates are cut again, he says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Turkey's Lira Deposit Scheme Could Backfire\par \par \uc2 1031 GMT - Turkey's new scheme that protects lira deposits against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations could backfire, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  on Monday said the government would compensate lira deposit holders if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declines more than the interest rate offered by banks. "If Erdogan's pledge is challenged, and the lira loses value, someone will have to pick up the tab," \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  strategist Bas van Geffen says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have worsened \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's already low foreign reserves, potentially eroding the credibility that the president can compensate for losses if the lira faced new headwinds, he says. The government's finances are also now even more linked to the lira's performance, which could exacerbate shocks if credibility risks materialize, he says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Scale of Turkish Lira Rebound Shows How Undervalued It Had Become\par \par \uc2 1028 GMT - The scale of the Turkish lira's rebound following measures designed to encourage people to hold deposits in lira rather than foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows how undervalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had become, \uc2 MUFG\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst \uc2 Lee Hardman\uc2  says. The substantial rebound "reflects in large part that lira weakness had recently significantly overshot fundamentals as it became deeply undervalued," he says. The measures should "at least temporarily" push the lira higher and should help slow further lira weakness going forward "by discouraging dollarisation flows in the Turkish economy." However, selling should resume as a fundemantal lack of confidence in policymaking in Turkey--which has cut interest rates despite high inflation--"remains in place," Hardman says. USD/TRY last trades at 12.5895, sharply down from Monday's record high of 18.3674, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Turkish Lira Selling Could Resume as Long as Erdogan Favors Low Rates\par \par \uc2 1021 GMT - The Turkish lira recovered a substantial chunk of its recent losses late Monday after measures to encourage depositors to hold savings in lira, but selling could soon resume as long as President Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  favors low interest rates, Victoria Scholar, head of investment at \uc2 Interactive Investor\uc2  , says. The government has said it will make up for losses incurred by holders of lira deposits if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declines exceed interest rates promised by banks. However, Erdogan "is showing no signs of shifting away from his stance in favour of ultra-loose monetary policy, despite spiralling inflation, which should continue to keep the lira under pressure." USD/TRY last trades at 12.6174, sharply lower compared with Monday's record high of 18.3674, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Turkish Lira's Gains on New Scheme May Not Last\par \par \uc2 1002 GMT - The Turkish lira's recovery after President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  announced measures to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't last unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverses course by raising interest rates, \uc2 Swissquote Bank\uc2  analyst Ipek Ozkardeskaya says. The government's pledge to compensate for losses in lira deposits resulting from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declines "should be taken with a pinch of salt," Ozkardeskaya says. It will "hardly convince investors to take the risk of sitting on the shaky lira, and will inevitably weigh on the budget," she says. Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep rates low even as inflation surges, she says. "Markets' tolerance for the low-rate policy won't be infinite, and the wind could rapidly change direction." USD/TRY falls 9.8% to 12.1208. On Monday, USD/TRY hit a record high of 18.3674, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Erdogan's Measures to Prop Up Lira May Fail\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT - President Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  's new measures to bolster the beleaguered lira may prove unsuccessful, BDSwiss Group analyst Marshall Gittler says. Erdogan on Monday announced a scheme that encourages Turks to hold savings in liras rather than dollars by offering protection against exchange rate fluctuations, causing a strong rebound in the lira. The government will make up for losses incurred by holders of lira deposits if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declines exceed interest rates promised by banks. "Of course what this means is that the government will print up more money and give it to deposit holders, thereby fuelling the inflation that's causing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to decline in the first place," Gittler says.(renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Turkish Lira Recovers After Erdogan Attempts to Bolster \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 0837 GMT - The Turkish lira recovers versus the dollar after President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  announced measures to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. Late Monday Erdogan unveiled a scheme aimed at encouraging Turkish residents to hold their savings in liras rather than dollars. That eased pressure on the lira, which recovered strongly after hitting an all-time low on Monday after Erdogan on Sunday cited Islam as a reason for not raising interest rates. "We are quite doubtful this is the end to the current lira story," \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  analyst Lars Sparreso Lykke Merklin says. USD/TRY is last up 0.2% at 13.4850 after earlier hitting a near four-week low of 11.8450, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . The pair had reached a record high of 18.3674 on Monday before Erdogan's latest announcement. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 21, 2021 07:15 ET (12:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020211221ehcl00150\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
