\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkish Lira Cuts its Collapse with a Record 50% Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionism\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  has triggered a sharp upward turn in the lira's value. If in recent months the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had starred in dizzying declines, the rise triggered since yesterday exceeds all historical records.\par \par \uc2 The free fall of the lira yesterday triggered new historical lows. The additional plunge of close to 10% broke the barrier of 20 units per euro for the first time. At its lowest levels of the day the community \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came close to 20.5 lira.\par \par \uc2 The turnaround in its price coincided with the messages announced by the country's president. Erdogan, the main promoter of the rate cuts against the tide that have sunk the value of the lira, announced yesterday new measures to try to alleviate the collapse of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  without having to resort to rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 The initiative with the greatest impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to analysts, is the promise to establish a kind of guarantee on lira deposits, through compensation, to avoid possible losses caused by the collapse of the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The aim of this measure is to avoid the 'dollarization' of the country, to ensure that citizens do not have to change the lira to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the case of further collapses of the lira. The country's banking employers assured that the announcement had an immediate response, which will materialize through sales of up to US$ 1 billion.\par \par \uc2 Purchases of the lira have boomed so suddenly that they have multiplied the upward pressure on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rally has been further accelerated by the unwinding of the bearish rally. Investors who had been short the lira, after accumulating months of extraordinary profitability, were forced to close their short positions in the face of the magnitude of the rises.\par \par \uc2 The multiplier effect of the huge bearish positions led to final rises of 25% yesterday on the same day that the lira fell as much as 10% at the start of the day.\par \par \uc2 The upward spiral continues in today's session, with intraday highs at 13.3 units per euro. In less than 24 hours, the lira has gone from 0.048 euros to 0.079 euros. With these records, the rise exceeds 50% from yesterday's lows, a record revaluation.\par \par \uc2 The soaring lira is paving the way for \uc2 Garanti Bank\uc2 , the Turkish bank controlled by \uc2 BBVA\uc2 , to rise on the \uc2 Istanbul Stock Exchange\uc2 . The Spanish bank also joins the rises in the Ibex.\par \par \uc2 Before this historic turnaround, the lira had plunged 45% in the last six weeks, with analysts warning of the heterodox monetary policy adopted by the country, at the behest of its president, Erdogan, an avowed enemy of rate hikes. With last Thursday's cut, the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced rates by 500 basis points since September despite an inflation rate close to 20% in the country and forecasts of CPI rises close to 30%.\par \par \uc2 Read\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211221ehcl007wo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
