\par\par \b \uc2 Turkish Lira, Stocks Sink Amid Inflation Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Caitlin Ostroff and Jared Malsin \par \uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2021\par 01:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Istanbul's stock market was twice forced to halt trading and the Turkish lira continued to fall Friday as concerns deepened that recent interest-rate cuts could cause an inflationary spiral.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's benchmark \uc2 Borsa Istanbul\uc2  100 index sank 8.5% Friday in its worst day since March, triggering two circuit breakers that halted trades. The lira lost as much as 8% of its value against the dollar, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest the decline in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The crash followed another decision by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to cut interest rates under pressure from President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , who favors lower rates as a part of a vision to grow the Turkish economy. Mainstream economists have urged the government to raise interest rates to control Turkey's rising inflation, which reached more than 21% last month, according to official statistics.\par \par \uc2 The lira's continuing decline is increasingly squeezing ordinary Turks, who have seen their savings evaporate. It is also adding to pressure on the banking system, which has high levels of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated loans to repay within the next 12 months. As of September, the loans equaled about 11% of Turkey's gross domestic product, according to \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are astonished to watch the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  releasing its precious \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  resources to the market today after it cut rates yesterday," said Erdal Bahcivan, chairman of the board of the Istanbul Chamber of Industry, in a tweet.\par \par \uc2 Friday's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was the fifth time that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped in to prop up the lira this month. It cited "unhealthy price formations in exchange rates," in a statement declaring the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Economists estimate that \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has more foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities than assets, giving it little firepower to steady the lira through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling assets Friday after the lira fell past 17 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to slide again hours later.\par \par \uc2 "The diminishing impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is really telling," said \uc2 Paul McNamara\uc2 , an emerging-market fund manager at GAM. "With this kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the trouble is the market knows the level of reserves they have. It's not like Russia or Brazil -- countries that really have a lot of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  they can throw at this."\par \par \uc2 The lira has lost more than half its purchasing power against the dollar this year, much of that decline in the past month, a dramatic unraveling reminiscent of past emerging-market crises in places such as Argentina and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 The plummeting lira makes it more likely that Turkey will need to implement capital controls -- measures to restrict or even prohibit the flow of money out of the country -- to keep the lira from being heavily sold, Mr. McNamara said.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's ability to impose such controls is complicated by the country's consistent need for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as banks and companies need to repay or service debts. Investors see few other options for Turkey to stabilize the lira, expecting that Mr. Erdogan won't want to raise interest rates. The Turkish president has fired a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors and other senior officials who opposed his unorthodox view of the economy.\par \par \uc2 The loss of confidence in Turkey's monetary policy has also put pressure on other parts of the market.\par \par \uc2 Turkish stocks had seen a strong run before Friday. Locals might have preferred to put their savings into stocks rather than other assets as inflation has risen, investors said, because companies can increase prices alongside inflation, boosting returns.\par \par \uc2 "Generally, a little bit of inflation is good for equities," said Daniel Wood, a portfolio manager at William Blair Investment Management. "Once you get concerned about hyperinflation, that's bad for companies."\par \par \uc2 Shortly after Thursday's rate raise, Mr. Erdogan also announced an increase in Turkey's minimum wage, which could also stoke inflation, Mr. Wood said. Concerns over unbridled inflation might have prompted some investors to sell shares.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring against default on $10,000 of five-year Turkish dollar-denominated bonds using derivatives contracts called credit default swaps climbed to about $525 a year Friday, from about $380 a year at the end of June, according to FactSet. Investors buy these swaps if they think the price for insuring against a default will rise further.\par \par \uc2 "The upheaval in the markets and the level that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached worries many of our companies and affects them negatively," said Rifat Hisarciklioglu, president of the Union of Chambers and Commodity Exchanges of Turkey.\par \par \uc2 Write to Caitlin Ostroff at caitlin.ostroff@wsj.com and Jared Malsin at jared.malsin@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 20-12-21 0016GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020211220ehck00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
