\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkey crisis: Istanbul stock market suffers biggest fall since March after Turkish lira plunges\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The BIST-100 index, selective of the \uc2 Istanbul Stock Exchange\uc2 , closed Friday's session with a fall of 8.52% to 2,084.47 points, after an eventful day in which trading has been interrupted twice by the collapse of the market as a result of the collapse of the Turkish lira.\par \par \uc2 The circuit breaker \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in barely an hour in response to the 5% and then 7% drop in the BIST-100 index, which finally fell 8.52% at the close of trading, the biggest drop since last March.\par \par \uc2 Despite this plunge in Friday's session, the BIST-100 in Turkish lira terms is currently more than 41% above the level recorded at the close of last year, although in dollar terms it would be down around 35%.\par \par \uc2 The shocks on the Ottoman trading floor have occurred in parallel to the collapse that one more day has experienced the lira, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey\uc2  yesterday cut interest rates by another 100 basis points to 14%, extending to 500 basis points the cut in the price of money since last September.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market to prop up the exchange rate of the lira, which marked this Friday new historic lows, in what is the fifth defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the institution so far in December.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market through sales transactions due to unhealthy price formations in exchange rates," the entity confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's value against the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared Friday to a record 17.1420 liras, up from yesterday's close of 15.6674 liras.\par \par \uc2 On Dec. 1, the date of the Ottoman \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar cross had reached almost 14 liras. On December 31, 2020, each dollar was exchanged for 7.43 lira.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee on Thursday decided to cut the benchmark interest rate for one-week refinancing auctions by 100 basis points to 14 percent.\par \par \uc2 This is the fourth consecutive cut in the benchmark interest rate applied by the Ottoman \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lowered the price of money to 14% from 19% in early September, despite upward pressure from inflation, which reached 21.31% in November.\par \par \uc2 However, the issuing institution hinted in its statement the end of the cycle of rate cuts by noting that it decided to complete the use of the limited space implied by the "transitory effects" on the prices of supply-side factors and other factors outside the control of monetary policy to reduce the rate, adding that it will assess in the first quarter of 2022 "the cumulative impact of recent decisions".\par \par \uc2 "During this period, all aspects of the policy framework will be reassessed to lay the foundations for sustainable price stability," he said.\par \par \uc2 (With information from EuropaPress)\par \par \uc2 Continue reading:\par \par \uc2 Turkey: lira wobbles after Erdogan appoints loyalist official with no economic background as finance minister\par \par \uc2 Turkey's finance minister resigns amid lira plunge crisis\par \par \uc2 Turkey condemned by \uc2 European Court of Human Rights\uc2  for arresting judges after failed 2016 coup\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211217ehch008ls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
