\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkey - The collapse of the lira forces the  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  again\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 MADRID, 17 (EUROPA PRESS) The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market to prop up the exchange rate of the lira, which marked this Friday new historic lows, in what is the fifth defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the institution so far in December. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market through sales transactions due to unhealthy price formations in exchange rates," the entity has confirmed. The dollar against the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared Friday to a record 17.1420 liras, compared to yesterday's close of 15.6674 liras. Last December 1, the date of the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Ottoman \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar cross had reached almost 14 liras. On December 31, 2020, each dollar was exchanged for 7.43 liras. The Monetary Policy Committee of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey decided on Thursday to cut the benchmark interest rate for one-week refinancing auctions by 100 basis points to 14%.\par \par \uc2  This is the fourth consecutive cut in the benchmark interest rate applied by the Ottoman \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lowered the price of money to 14% from 19% in early September, despite upward pressure from inflation, which reached 21.31% in November. However, the Ottoman issuer in its statement hinted at the end of the cycle of rate cuts by noting that it decided to complete the use of limited space involving the "transitory effects" on prices of supply-side factors and other factors outside the control of monetary policy to reduce the rate, adding that it will assess in the first quarter of 2022 "the cumulative impact of recent decisions". "During this period, all aspects of the policy framework will be reassessed to lay the foundations for sustainable price stability," it said.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211217ehch0070s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
