\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkey: Turkish lira hits record lows on expectations of a new rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 MADRID, 13 (EUROPA PRESS) The quotation of the Turkish lira against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply on Monday in anticipation of a further cut in the benchmark interest rate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey\uc2 , whose Monetary Policy Committee will meet on Thursday. Thus, the cross between the dollar and the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood before the opening of markets in the Old Continent in 14.4640 liras for each 'greenback', a new record low, compared to 13.8774 liras previous closing. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again last Friday in the market to prop up the exchange rate of the lira, which was the third defense of the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the institution so far in December. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market through sales transactions due to unhealthy price formations in exchange rates," confirmed the entity. Last December 1, the date of the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Ottoman \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar crossing had reached almost 14 liras.\par \par \uc2  On December 31, 2020, each dollar was exchanged for 7.43 liras, so far this year the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen almost half of its value vanish. In recent weeks, the collapse of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been aggravated after comments by its president, \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , that the country was waging an "economic war". The lira also recorded negative developments after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by 100 basis points in mid-November, bringing to 400 basis points the decline in the price of money since the summer. On the other hand, the country's year-on-year inflation rate climbed to 21.31% in November, up from 19.89% in October and well above the 14.03% in November 2020.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211213ehcd0014h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
