\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Turkey \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  again in the market to support the lira\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  today \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the market to prop up the exchange rate of the lira, in what is the third defense of the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the institution so far in December. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market through sales transactions due to unhealthy price formations in exchange rates," said the monetary institution, as reported by the agency Europa Press. The dollar exchange rate had risen today to 13.9549 Turkish liras, but later eased to 13.8862 liras, when last Wednesday, the date of the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Eurasian country, the dollar cross also reached almost 14 liras. On December 31, 2020 dollars were exchanged for 7.43 liras, so so far this year the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen almost half of its value vanish. In recent weeks the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge has been exacerbated by comments from President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  that the country was waging an "economic war".\par \par \uc2  The lira also recorded negative developments after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by 100 basis points in mid-November, and on the other hand, the country's year-on-year inflation rate climbed to 21.31% in November, compared to 19.89% in October and well above the 14.03% in November 2020. (T\u233\'00\'E9lam)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211210ehca00bdk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw94\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1410\pichgoal600
