\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  comes to the rescue of the lira again after strong inflation figures\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Friday in the market to prop up the exchange rate of the lira, in what is the second defense of the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the institution so far this week. This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes after inflation data that has surprised on the upside in the Ottoman country.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market through sale transactions due to unhealthy price formations in exchange rates," the institution has confirmed.\par \par \uc2 In a nutshell, the Turkish bank comes to the defense of the lira using its dollar reserves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertakes to drain some of the lira supply in the market (investors or agents who want to sell the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) by offering in exchange dollars or other 'hard' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that make up the reserves accumulated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This may temporarily reduce the downward pressure on the exchange rate, as the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has limited reserves (estimated at around $50 billion).\par \par \uc2 The only way to prevent the lira from depreciating further without resorting to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is through interest rate hikes or structural reforms to improve the country's competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  The dollar exchange rate had risen as high as 13.8898 Turkish liras on Friday, but later eased to 13.7244 liras. Last Wednesday, the dollar cross reached almost 14 liras, forcing the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Dec. 31, 2020, dollars were trading at 7.43 liras, so so far this year the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen almost half of its value vanish.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge has been exacerbated by comments from President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  that the country was waging an "economic war". The lira also saw negative developments after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by 100 basis points in mid-November.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Turkish Statistical Institute (TurkStat) announced that the country's year-on-year inflation rate climbed to 21.31% in November, up from 19.89% in October and well above the 14.03% in November 2020.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211203ehc3005yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
