\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkish finance minister resigns amid lira slump crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Ankara, Dec 2 (EFE) - Turkey's Finance Minister \uc2 Lutfi Elvan\uc2  resigned Thursday in the midst of the crisis of devaluation of the lira, which lost 30% of its value last month, while the country's President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  continues to defend a policy of low interest rates. Turkish media report that Elvan's departure had been expected for weeks, as the former minister had been privately rejecting Erdogan's monetary strategy and his continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the work of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .Elvan's resignation and the appointment of the new minister, Nureddin Nebati, until now deputy finance minister, was published after midnight in the official state gazette, with a decree signed by the president. The document notes that the resigning minister requested to be relieved of the post and that his request was accepted by Erdogan.Nebati is the third finance minister since November, when Erdogan's son-in-law Berat Albayrak resigned from the post.\par \par \uc2  At the opening of the Turkish market today, the lira fell 1.47% against the dollar and 1.75% against the euro, trading at 13.52 and 15.31 respectively against those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .Last November was the worst in the history of the Turkish lira, with a cumulative loss of nearly 30%. The Turkish media had been speculating two weeks ago with the resignation of Elvan for what they claim was his opposition to Erdogan's strategy of keeping interest rates low, arguing, contrary to the opinion of most economists, that this helps to combat inflation, which is at 20%. "We have abandoned the policy of high interest rates and have moved to a strategy of growth by investment, employment and production," said the president yesterday in a speech to his party, the Islamist AKP, in power since 2002.The devaluation of the lira is affecting the purchasing power of the Turks and in recent days there have been demonstrations and protests against the government, while the opposition calls for early elections. The Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared yesterday by 10% against the euro and the dollar immediately after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through sales to influence the exchange value of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211202ehc2003xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
