\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Turkish Lira Continues to Fall and Reaches an All-Time High against the Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Istanbul, Oct 12 (EFE) - The Turkish lira marked Tuesday for the first time a value of 9 units per U.S. dollar, its lowest point since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform in 2005, in line with the downward path that follows since the beginning of last September. The sharp fall of the lira in the last 12 hours is also observed against the euro, although in this case has not yet reached the level of 10.5 units per euro recorded last June, although it is close to 10.45 units.Turkish analysts link today's decline with the speech of the governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sahap Kavcioglu, on Monday, when he defended the decision to lower interest rates from 19% to 18%, taken on September 23.\par \par \uc2  The move came as a surprise to financial markets, which did not expect a rate cut when the year-on-year inflation rate stands at 19.25%.Turkish President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  has insisted for years on keeping rates low, saying that, contrary to what economists believe, high interest rates accelerate inflation rather than curb it. Some analysts link the lira's new decline to a speech by Erdogan yesterday, in which he promised to "do whatever it takes in Syria," which is interpreted in the Turkish press as a possible signal of a new military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in that country, where \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls several border areas.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211012ehac0040h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
