\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW-Turkish markets tumble after Erdogan axes  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief\b0\par\par\uc2 936 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds views)\par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 22 (Reuters) - Turkey's lira and financial markets fell on Monday after the weekend sacking of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor. It left major investment banks and fund managers reassessing their views on Turkey, with some wondering whether severe crisis measures such as capital controls would be needed.\par \par \uc2 Turkish Finance Minister \uc2 Lutfi Elvan\uc2  said on Monday that Turkey was determined to stick to free-market rules and a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.\par \par \uc2 JP MORGAN\par \par \uc2 "In the midst of tightening global financial conditions, which could well turn disruptive, any premature easing or reference to that could undermine hard-earned policy credibility.\par \par \uc2 "For now, we are not changing any forecast and await further guidance from the CBRT (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and data. We are currently MW (neutral) local bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the GBI-EM Model Portfolio, having taken profits on our bullish TRY options position."\par \par \uc2 SOCIETE GENERALE\par \par \uc2 "A\u287\'01\'1Fbal's dismissal leaves \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the point of no return"\par \par \uc2 * Dollarisation and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resume.\par \par \uc2 * Considering the shortage of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, we may see more financial regulatory \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Foreign investors will exit Turkish assets.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon be headed toward another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 * Battle royale ahead between policy-makers and the market.\par \par \uc2 DEUTSCHE BANK\par \par \uc2 "Given the fact that the CBT (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) had yet to significantly rebuild reserves since last year\u8217\'20\'19s crisis, the market will be sceptical of a repeat of last year\u8217\'20\'19s policy to contain TRY weakness using reserve drawdown. It is likely our forecasts on interest rates, inflation and growth have to be reassessed."\par \par \uc2 ASHMORE\par \par \uc2 "The leopard has not changed its spots. Erdogan remains a populist authoritarian, whose understanding of macroeconomics is non-existent," said \uc2 Jan Dehn\uc2 , head of research at \uc2 Ashmore Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The issue is that the dynamics above will hit a population that is suffering with inflation. For how long will the average man in the street and the elite of merchants and businessmen tolerate the situation?"\par \par \uc2 SEB\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will respond with ad-hoc statements and measures to stabilise the TRY, using swap transactions and drawing on state-owned banks to sell dollars, but these are short-term instruments to smooth out short-term market moves.\par \par \uc2 "They don\u8217\'20\'19t rebuild the credibility of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has been severely damaged by political influence. The authorities will be left with two choices, either pledge to use interest rates to stabilise markets, or to impose capital controls."\par \par \uc2 "Given the increasingly authoritarian approach that President Erdogan has taken, capital controls \u8211\'20\'13 such as limitations and taxes on earnings remittances and curbs on the ability of locals to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - are the most likely choice. They will intend for such restrictions to remain for a limited time, but that time may last for years."\par \par \uc2 SAXO BANK\par \par \uc2 "It's a risky business when you have no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," Saxo's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy \uc2 John Hardy\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "If they move rates (lower) again and if the lira moves again, then my chief concern would be that you get some form of capital controls."\par \par \uc2 BARCLAYS\par \par \uc2 "The removal of the market-friendly governor is likely to hurt policy credibility in our view. In a scenario of a reversal of the past four months\u8217\'20\'19 portfolio inflows of $10bn and/or restart of dollarisation, we may see a major spike in volatility, probably resulting in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies again."\par \par \uc2 NORDEA\par \par \uc2 "We will NEVER turn bullish on TRY as long as Erdogan is effectively running the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," global chief strategist Andreas Steno Larsen tweeted.\par \par \uc2 TENEO\par \par \uc2 "Predictably, noise (coming solely from outside Turkey) about capital controls is back. As we stressed in the past, outright capital controls are far too politically toxic in the Turkish context; this is true even for President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s regime."\par \par \uc2 SCOPE RATINGS\par \par \uc2 "Official reserves could see downside risk as well due to renewed capital outflows and a wider current-account deficit. Reserves had not recovered from damage done over recent years with net foreign assets ex-short-term swaps of negative $53 billion as of January (an all-time low), so a fresh drop in reserve stocks increases the risk around a balance-of-payment crisis."\par \par \uc2 MORGAN STANLEY\par \par \uc2 "Turkey cash spreads are 150-250 bp (basis points) tighter across the curve, with nearly two-thirds of the move happening in the second week of November as markets built up expectations of likely stabilisation of macro parameters such as \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Accordingly, we think that if markets are concerned about policy reversal we are likely to see an unwind of the move, i.e., spreads widen by 125-150 bp in the near term, and should those tail-risk expectations materialise we can have another 100-150 bp move wider in spreads. Such a move would not only pare back the gains since November but would look worse off on a relative basis \u8211\'20\'13 as EMBI itself if 52 bp tighter."\par \par \uc2 VANGUARD\uc2  ASSET MANAGEMENT\par \par \uc2 "External funding needs are still very high as the CAD (current account deficit) widens with oil \u8211\'20\'13 and the capital account is dominated by short-term flows that must be rolled," said Nick Eisinger, principal for fixed income emerging markets at \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 . NR (non-resident) holdings of Turk GB (government bonds) is low but capital outflows emanate elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 "Household deposit dollarisation will likely continue, spiking further USD demand and hitting the lira.\par \par \uc2 "So far, we do not see any deposit flight out of the country- that is a key trigger."\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Marc Jones and Tom Arnold; editing by Kevin Liffey, Larry King)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-25T11:54:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210322eh3m01xah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
