\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  eye best week in 5 months as Biden edges closer to victory\b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2020\par 10:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * MSCI's EM stocks index rises 6% this week\par \par \uc2 * Rouble weakens as Biden edges close to winning U.S. vote\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  top $100 bln year-to-date - GS\par \par \uc2 By Shreyashi Sanyal\par \par \uc2 Nov 6 (Reuters) - Emerging market stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were set for their best weekly gains in five months on Friday, as Democratic candidate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  inched close to winning a tight U.S. election that has also weakened bets for a major U.S. fiscal stimulus.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's index for emerging market stocks has risen 6% so far this week, while \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are up 1.3%, driven by Asian and other markets seen as benefiting from the potential departure of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso, sensitive to Trump's drive to keep jobs in the United States and impose more tariffs on trade, has gained 2% this week while China's yuan has seen its best performance in a month, gaining more than 1%.\par \par \uc2 "The large bounce in equities this week creates an opportunity for investors to reassess and rebalance their portfolios in preparation for a President Biden and divided Congress," said Mark Haefele, chief investment officer at UBS Global Wealth Management.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of a divided Congress has also strengthened expectations that the burden of economic stimulus over the months ahead would remain with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and other central banks funnelling yet more cash into the financial system.\par \par \uc2 The more bonds the Fed buys, the more tends to trickle to higher-yielding emerging markets like Indonesia, South Africa or Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Russia's rouble, expected to weaken if Trump loses the presidency, has been bolstered by oil prices this week. It was down 0.4% against the dollar on Friday but up almost 3% this week.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira, which has struggled for months, shed 0.3% and was on track for its tenth weekly loss, after a media report said \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister \uc2 Berat Albayrak\uc2  ruled out an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  estimated \b \highlight22\uc2 Turkey\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent $101 billion to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  say credit supply in emerging markets dropped significantly this week, but expect a pick-up in the coming weeks, given the conducive market backdrop, "with expectations of $25 billion worth of sovereign supply and around $5 billion worth of quasi sovereign supply materializing before end of the year."\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint dropped against the euro, leading declines among Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the Czech crown edged lower against the euro a day after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates as expected.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance in 2020, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2  For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance in 2020, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2OusNdX}}}\par \par \uc2 For TOP NEWS across emerging markets\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see (Reporting by Shreyashi Sanyal in Bengaluru; Editing by Shailesh Kuber) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-6T10:47:55.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201106egb601lhi\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Turkey near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15